    overview: "The highest and rarest truthfulness is in the levels of religion: fear, hope, reverence, doing without, contentment, trust and love. Each has a beginning, which earns the name, and a reality, which is its end. A man afraid of a robber goes pale and cannot sleep. He says he fears the Fire and sins calmly. The Prophet saw Gabriel fill the horizon and fainted.",
